ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20204, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JZbSSAtX3H5hrhLphii3PE", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20204, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016zR6aRQkCjFwEYVJQkBPUx", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20504, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016zR6aRQkCjFwEYVJQkBPUx", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20504, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016zR6aRQkCjFwEYVJQkBPUx", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25259, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FWF59AEAg47FLcjpFZWT34", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so for a while the regions ran different versions. A second attempt finished in all regions. checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 everywhere, passing health checks, with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the rollout orchestrator error, and check why v2.3.1 went to production after the RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55859, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FWF59AEAg47FLcjpFZWT34", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55859, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FWF59AEAg47FLcjpFZWT34", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57202, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GwrK4dxkXXB27a4wTUBwAA", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57502, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GwrK4dxkXXB27a4wTUBwAA", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57502, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GwrK4dxkXXB27a4wTUBwAA", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62577, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in every region, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with about an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Since it had been healthy before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt failed with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so the regions briefly ran different versions. I retried the same rollback and it finished in all regions.\n- checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, passing health checks, with about a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out, but the incident list shows INC-0001 was created. I didn't retry, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- It's titled \"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0\". The summary describes the failure, both rollback attempts and the current state.\n- It lists three follow-ups:\n  - find out why v2.3.1 failed\n  - look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback\n  - find out why v2.3.1 reached production after its release candidate failed in staging", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NsMZWe7hkvjbq2PvCdKhdL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0123gxkz1L6GughU9F174wpM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Nigv4UG4sPjCU2JHZzTrbP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LSiMhaxrNHG1wxWTwy145c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back. Rolling back again is safe because it targets the same version, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QmcFMpD9LeJnx7G1nF8bPA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JZbSSAtX3H5hrhLphii3PE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016zR6aRQkCjFwEYVJQkBPUx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FWF59AEAg47FLcjpFZWT34", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so for a while the regions ran different versions. A second attempt finished in all regions. checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 everywhere, passing health checks, with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the rollout orchestrator error, and check why v2.3.1 went to production after the RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GwrK4dxkXXB27a4wTUBwAA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in every region, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with about an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Since it had been healthy before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt failed with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so the regions briefly ran different versions. I retried the same rollback and it finished in all regions.\n- checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, passing health checks, with about a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out, but the incident list shows INC-0001 was created. I didn't retry, so there's only one incident and one page.\n- It's titled \"checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0\". The summary describes the failure, both rollback attempts and the current state.\n- It lists three follow-ups:\n  - find out why v2.3.1 failed\n  - look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback\n  - find out why v2.3.1 reached production after its release candidate failed in staging", "type": "text"}]}]}